 ### CLM
-CLM is a training optimization for 3D Gaussian Splatting that removes the GPU memory barrier by offloading Gaussian states to CPU memory and overlapping CPU-side optimizer updates with GPU rendering [7351-clm.md]. It solves the problem of VRAM exhaustion and communication stalls in large-scale scenes by implementing a smart caching policy that keeps frequently updated Gaussians on the GPU while streaming others [7351-clm.md]. Unlike baseline offloading which incurs significant latency, CLM uses pipelining and early Adam updates to hide communication overhead, enabling training of scenes that exceed GPU memory on a single device [7351-clm.md].
+CLM is a training optimization for 3D Gaussian Splatting that removes the GPU memory barrier by offloading Gaussian states to CPU memory and overlapping CPU-side optimizer updates with GPU rendering [G]. It solves the problem of VRAM exhaustion and communication stalls in large-scale scenes by implementing a smart caching policy that keeps frequently updated Gaussians on the GPU while streaming others [G]. Unlike baseline offloading which incurs significant latency, CLM uses pipelining and early Adam updates to hide communication overhead, enabling training of scenes that exceed GPU memory on a single device [G].
 
 ### FastGS
-FastGS is a general acceleration framework for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that significantly reduces training time by regulating the number of Gaussians based on multi-view consistency, dispensing with explicit budgeting mechanisms [9177-fastgs.md]. It re-engineers the training loop using dynamic sparse rasterization and fast gradient checkpointing to skip negligible computations [9177-fastgs.md]. Unlike sibling methods that rely on Gaussian-associated properties (Taming-3DGS) or indirect gradient approximations (Speedy-Splat), FastGS directly evaluates each Gaussian's contribution to multi-view reconstruction quality to guide densification and pruning [9177-fastgs.md].
